    "title": "You can get a free Frosty, fries at Wendy's on April 7. Here's how.",
    "text": "April 7, 2026, 11:05 a.m. ETDeeperDiveBETADeeperDive is a GenAI Answer Engine built for trusted publishers. It delivers clear answers and real-time content based on what people are reading now — showcasing various stories from the usatodaydemo Network that highlight not just what happened, but why it matters. This is currently a BETA being quality assessed by human beings. Mistakes may occur. Please reference surfaced articles to validate AI summaryWhat triggered Wendy's free Frosty and fries promotion on April 7?What triggered Wendy's free Frosty and fries promotion on April 7?How does Wendy's tie its promotions to March Madness events?Which NCAA players have NIL partnerships with Wendy's?AI Overview DeeperDive is a GenAI Answer Engine built for trusted publishers. It delivers clear answers and real-time content based on what people are reading now — showcasing various stories from the USA TODAY Network that highlight not just what happened, but why it matters. This is currently a BETA being quality assessed by human beings. Mistakes may occur. Please reference surfaced articles to validate AI summaryWendy's is offering a free small fries and a small chocolate or vanilla Frosty on April 7 at participating U.S. restaurants, a promotion tied to a dunk in the NCAA Men’s Basketball Championship game where Michigan defeated Connecticut 69-63. The fast‑food chain’s offer requires no purchase and highlights its NIL partnerships with players from both schools.There was a dunk during the NCAA Men's Basketball Championship Game on Monday night, April 6, which means Wendy's is giving away some freebies on Tuesday, April 7.Wendy's customers can score a free small order of fries paired with a free small chocolate or vanilla Frosty on April 7. The offer is available in-restaurant only at participating Wendy's locations in the U.S.There is no purchase necessary to redeem the offer, according to Wendy's.Wendy's free Frosty, free fry deal is due to NCAA championship game dunkThe national championship game Monday night featured the Michigan Wolverines facing off against the Connecticut Huskies. Wendy's has name, image and likeness (NIL) partnerships with Michigan players Yaxel Lendeborg, Elliot Cadeau, and Morez Johnson Jr., as well as Connecticut center Tarris Reed Jr.Michigan beat Connecticut 69-63 to clinch its second men's basketball championship in school history. The first came in 1989 when the Wolverines, led by head coach Steve Fisher, beat Seton Hall 80-79 in overtime.Gabe Hauari is a national trending news reporter at USA TODAY. You can follow him on X @GabeHauari or email him at Gdhauari@gannett.com.",
